// Copper `ws` standard library — minimal WebSocket client.
//
// `import { ... } from ws`. Pure Rust std (no dependencies): the RFC 6455
// handshake (Sec-WebSocket-Key / -Accept via inline SHA-1 + base64) and
// client frame masking are hand-rolled over a std TcpStream. Bundled as
// `pub mod ws { ... }` with std/ws_native.rs.
//
//   ws::request(url, message) -> first text reply (String, "" on error)
//   ws::send(url, message)    -> bool (connect, send one text frame, close)
//
// `url` is a plaintext WebSocket URL: "ws://host:port/path". Secure
// `wss://` (TLS) is NOT supported in this dependency-free build — it would
// require a TLS crate; use the `http` module for HTTPS request/response, or
// a TLS-terminating proxy in front of the socket.
